Feature: TC_20_STAFF - CISYF Late Penalty Payment Summary by Role E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Display Late penalty percentage for CISYF late penalty" (BISSAGL-5517, AT-TC-01 to 14,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14747 to 14732)
  # Rewritten 16-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   The Payments screen Payment Summary shows the BISS, CRISS and CISYF columns (with their amount columns) to every
  #   BISS staff role that may see payments; with all roles the Total DPS Payment equals BISS + CRISS + CISYF Net
  #   Payment Amount, and every Reduction Type row (Gross Claim to Net Payment Amount, Late Penalty included) is shown.
  #
  #   Sections 1-12: the SSO super admin (agr0043) gives test user agr0191 one role, agr0191 opens a payment herd's
  #   Payments screen and checks the three columns. Section 13: all roles, plus the Total DPS Payment check.
  #   Section 14: the Reduction Type columns and rows on the same herd.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - Selenium printed whether each heading and row existed; here a missing one fails the step, listing all missing.
  #   - AT-TC-12 repeated the AT-TC-11 role (BISS Risk Management 2 User) on the next herd; kept as in legacy.
  #   - AT-TC-13 and AT-TC-14 both used herd row 7 (2024); Section 14 re-opens the Section 13 herd.
  #   - Row names are matched by contained text, so the euro amounts in "Between ... 60,000-100,000" and "Amount
  #     Exceeding ... 100,000" are not needed in this file.
  #   - TC_09 and TC_15 also change agr0191's roles: do not run them at the same time as this pack.
  #
  # Test data:
  #   Herds from the database, as in legacy ("Get Herds With Payments", scheme years 2023 and 2024).
  #   Logins agr0043 (SSO super admin) and agr0191 (the user whose roles change). Password: TD:Password from the
  #   TestData row of this test case, the same for both.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (SSO Administration, Payments)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @regression @staff @payments @roles @sso @cisyf @e2e
